            "english_quote": "The evil one, however, knowing that we are eager to sow",
            "issue": "The draft treats our effort as the inferred content of the evil one's knowledge. That is a defensible contextual interpretation, but it is not disclosed. The Greek instead explicitly uses a genitive absolute, which permits the straightforward circumstantial reading “knowing [this], while we are eager …”; the preceding claim about affection's sufficiency for salvation supplies a natural alternative object of knowledge. The two readings differ in what the evil one is said to know and in how the competing efforts are related.",
